[:option {:value "19016138"} "Kayak Doubles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016157"} "Kayak Fours, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016169"} "Canadian Singles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016188"} "Canadian Doubles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016207"} "Kayak Singles, 200 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016226"} "Kayak Singles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016245"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016264"} "Kayak Fours, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016276"} "Canadian Singles, 200 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19016295"} "Canadian Doubles, 500 metres, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "307065"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "353450"} "2016"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/989"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Kayak Singles, 200 metres, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "4 –  5 August 2021"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2129"} "Sea Forest Waterway, 6-44, 3chome, Uminomori, Koto-ku, Tokyo Bay, Tokyo, Japan"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/19016100"} "25 from 19 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "This was the third and last appearance of the event for a while, as it will be not part of the canoe sprint programme in 2024. The 2016 Olympic champion and reigning world champion, " [:a {:href "/athletes/123211"} "Liam Heath"] " of Great Britain, was the clear favourite over this distance. His main contenders were " [:a {:href "/athletes/124653"} "Maxime Beaumont"] " of France, silver medallist in Rio, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/116612"} "Saul Craviotto"] " of Spain, the bronze medallist in 2016 and silver medallist at London four years earlier. The reigning European champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/136538"} "Sándor Tótka"] " of Hungary was another favourite."] "\n\n" [:p {} "From the five preliminary rounds, 10 athletes directly qualified into the semi-finals, while the others had one more round in the quarter-finals. In his race, Heath finished only third but easily won his quarter-final with an Olympic Record time. Both semi-finals were won by Hungarians, Tótka and 25-year-old " [:a {:href "/athletes/143675"} "Kolos Csizmadia"] ", who beat Heath into second place. In the A Final, Tótka enjoyed a sensational victory in beating " [:a {:href "/athletes/134602"} "Manfredi Rizza"] " of Italy and Heath. This was the fourth Olympic medal for the British canoeist after securing a bronze (K-1 200) and a silver (K-2 200) at London 2012, and a gold (K-1 200) at the 2016 Rio Olympics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Tótka and his wife had moved to a lakeside cottage as soon as the Covid pandemic broke out, and he continued his training and preparations, knowing that the Olympics would eventually return."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "135"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/136538"} "Sándor Tótka"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "35.070 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "35.114 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "35.035 (1 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} 